35	WhatsApp Launches Parent-Managed Accounts to Enhance Pre-Teen Safety	WhatsApp Launches Parent-Managed Accounts to Enhance Pre-Teen Safety	whatsapp-launches-parent-managed-accounts-to-enhance-pre-teen-safety	<p>In a significant move aimed at bolstering online safety for younger users, WhatsApp has officially introduced parent-managed accounts for children under the age of 13. This new feature allows guardians to link their WhatsApp accounts to their pre-teen's, granting them unprecedented control over their child's messaging experience on the popular platform.</p><p>The initiative comes amidst growing calls for stricter regulations and enhanced safety measures for children interacting with digital platforms. WhatsApp, owned by Meta, has long maintained an age restriction of 13 in many regions, but the reality of younger users accessing the app has spurred the company to develop a more secure framework.</p><h3>How Parent-Managed Accounts Work</h3><p>Under the new system, parents will be able to set up a WhatsApp account for their pre-teen and link it to their own. This linkage provides parents with crucial oversight capabilities, including:</p><ul><li><strong>Contact Approval:</strong> Guardians will have the authority to approve or deny new contacts for their child's account, ensuring interactions are limited to known and trusted individuals.</li><li><strong>Activity Monitoring:</strong> While direct message content remains encrypted and private, parents can access reports on their child's interactions, providing insight into who they are communicating with and how frequently.</li><li><strong>Privacy Settings Management:</strong> Parents can manage and adjust the privacy settings for their child's account, controlling aspects like profile visibility and group invitations.</li></ul><p>This approach aims to strike a balance between providing younger users with access to communication tools and safeguarding them from potential online risks.</p><h3>Addressing Youth Safety Concerns</h3><p>The introduction of these parent-managed accounts is a direct response to persistent concerns from parents, educators, and child safety advocates regarding the exposure of young children to inappropriate content, cyberbullying, and contact from strangers. By integrating parental controls directly into the platform, WhatsApp seeks to create a safer digital environment for its youngest users.</p><p>This also aligns with Meta's broader strategy to enhance youth safety across its suite of applications, including Instagram and Facebook. The company has faced scrutiny in the past over its impact on younger demographics, making this a proactive step to demonstrate its commitment to child protection.</p><p>The new feature is expected to roll out globally, empowering parents with the tools they need to guide their children's digital journeys responsibly and securely on one of the world's most widely used messaging applications.</p>	WhatsApp rolls out parent-managed accounts for pre-teens under 13, empowering guardians with tools to approve contacts and oversee activity, bolstering online safety.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1704383110020-86b408af4ac2?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHx3aGF0c2FwcCUyQyUyMGNoaWxkJTIwc2FmZXR5JTJDJTIwcGFyZW50YWwlMjBjb250cm9sfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3NzMzMjQ0MjV8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	TechCrunch	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxNdUl1bHVoYkJjVWI4YlZlY2hVaWJNZnJFSEdaRGxRUlYyc2JxNDdiUndrLVJ4QURySWNYdFNwRWp5Qlludm5yMEJHdnZpcVJYQnM5VDhSbllfZmdsYXNNOUExMTdfSDZTZmVLTk1UQlBVX2I1bFNVX0dJWVc3U3VvUXdsaE1rZmFHWkJOMGNYN3poRVdjallQUg?oc=5	\N	2026-03-12 14:07:05.221	2026-03-12 14:07:05.258276	Technology	38
