102	BYU Advances in Big 12 Tournament Behind Davis Jr.'s Dominant 20-Point Performance	BYU Advances in Big 12 Tournament Behind Davis Jr.'s Dominant 20-Point Performance	byu-advances-in-big-12-tournament-behind-davis-jrs-dominant-20-point-performance	<p>PROVO, UT – BYU's basketball team showcased a formidable performance in the Big 12 Tournament's second round, decisively defeating West Virginia University 68-48. The Cougars' triumph was largely fueled by a stellar individual effort from guard Kennard Davis Jr., who registered a season-high 20 points.</p><p>The victory propels BYU further into the tournament, underscoring their competitive strength in the challenging Big 12 conference. Davis Jr.'s offensive explosion proved to be the catalyst, as he efficiently found his rhythm and consistently contributed crucial points throughout the contest.</p><h3>Mountaineers Struggle to Find Offensive Footing</h3><p>For the West Virginia Mountaineers, the game proved to be an uphill battle, particularly on the offensive end. The team struggled significantly to generate scoring opportunities and maintain offensive consistency against BYU's staunch defense. This offensive drought contributed to their 20-point deficit and ultimately led to their elimination from the tournament.</p><p>While specific defensive statistics were not immediately available across all sources, the collective reporting indicates that BYU's defensive strategy effectively stifled West Virginia's key players and limited their shooting percentages.</p><h3>Tournament Implications and Future Outlook</h3><p>BYU's convincing win not only marks a significant achievement in their tournament run but also sends a clear message about their capabilities to remaining competitors. The team will look to carry this momentum into their next game as they aim for further advancement in the Big 12 Tournament.</p><p>For West Virginia, the loss concludes their tournament journey and will prompt a period of reflection and strategic planning for the future. The Mountaineers will undoubtedly be evaluating their performance, particularly their offensive execution, as they prepare for the next season.</p>	Kennard Davis Jr. delivered a season-high 20 points, spearheading BYU's commanding 68-48 victory over West Virginia in the Big 12 Tournament's second round, securing their advancement.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1653015503992-347de54a8125?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxiYXNrZXRiYWxsJTJDJTIwY29sbGVnZS1zcG9ydHMlMkMlMjB2aWN0b3J5fGVufDB8MHx8fDE3NzMzMzIzNjh8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	Deseret News, West Virginia University Athletics, BYU Athletics, WV MetroNews, Yahoo Sports	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQNkF5c09DZUFRSTlmSlFsdDduRG5yT1RGUV9kZVVDT2pSLS1BNjYwazM4TmpRdlE4Tk1UMkxOZm05SFZBcWJtY0xYUXczcmdPSm4weTNCQUdLa1FOYWtDTnpNR1NHb0FBeHVNT3NBVFZTMU5ocFRNaXJINl9VcVc0ajBaTG44ZnNBUlI2Q0FzeW1BVllGT0FhS1VkdFdOV2sxWS1qWEhySm9DalhQNmJSQWx0eW81UQ?oc=5	\N	2026-03-12 16:19:28.23	2026-03-12 16:19:28.264779	Business	37
698	Elon Musk Announces $20 Billion Terafab Chip Plant in Austin, Igniting AI Expansion	Elon Musk Announces $20 Billion Terafab Chip Plant in Austin, Igniting AI Expansion	elon-musk-announces-20-billion-terafab-chip-plant-in-austin-igniting-ai-expansion	<p>Austin, Texas is set to become an even greater nexus of technological innovation with Elon Musk's latest revelation: a colossal $20 billion investment into a Terafab chip manufacturing plant. This move marks a significant escalation in Musk's burgeoning artificial intelligence ambitions, positioning the Texas capital at the heart of future AI development.</p><p>While details surrounding the Terafab plant are still emerging, the sheer scale of the investment underscores Musk's commitment to vertical integration across his various ventures, particularly those heavily reliant on advanced computing power. Companies like Tesla, with its autonomous driving initiatives, and xAI, Musk's dedicated artificial intelligence startup, require a vast supply of high-performance chips to train and deploy their sophisticated models.</p><p><h3>Boosting Domestic Chip Production and AI Capacity</h3></p><p>The establishment of such a facility is poised to have multi-faceted impacts. Domestically, it will bolster semiconductor manufacturing capabilities, a critical sector that has seen increasing geopolitical and supply chain scrutiny. For Musk's ecosystem, it means greater control over the production of specialized AI chips, potentially reducing reliance on external foundries and accelerating the pace of innovation within his companies.</p><p>The term 'Terafab' itself suggests a facility capable of producing chips at an unprecedented scale, likely optimized for AI workloads that demand immense processing power and data throughput. This strategic investment in core infrastructure indicates a long-term vision for AI that goes beyond mere software development, delving deep into the hardware foundation that underpins intelligence.</p><p><h3>Austin's Growing Tech Footprint</h3></p><p>Austin, already home to Tesla's Gigafactory Texas and a burgeoning tech scene, solidifies its status as a pivotal hub for Musk's expansive enterprises. The new Terafab plant is expected to create thousands of high-skilled jobs, further stimulating the local economy and attracting a specialized workforce.</p><p>Musk's track record of ambitious, transformative projects suggests that this Terafab plant will not merely be an incremental addition to the chip industry but a bold attempt to redefine the scale and efficiency of AI-specific semiconductor production. As the global race for AI supremacy intensifies, this $20 billion investment signals a clear intent from Elon Musk to lead from the front, from the very silicon up.</p>	Elon Musk reveals plans for a monumental $20 billion Terafab chip manufacturing plant in Austin, Texas, significantly amplifying his ambitious pursuit of artificial intelligence dominance.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1716436330152-a58390897652?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxhcnRpZmljaWFsLWludGVsbGlnZW5jZSUyQyUyMGNoaXAtbWFudWZhY3R1cmluZyUyQyUyMGZhY3Rvcnl8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc3NDE4NTU1OXww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	KXAN Austin	https://news.google.?oc=5	\N	2026-03-22 13:19:19.858	2026-03-22 13:19:19.923444	AI	16
720	Sunday's Sizzling Start: Region Braces for Early Summer Warmth	Sunday's Sizzling Start: Region Braces for Early Summer Warmth	sundays-sizzling-start-region-braces-for-early-summer-warmth	<h3>Early Summer Preview: Unseasonably High Temperatures Expected This Sunday</h3>\n<p>Get ready to dust off those summer essentials a bit early! Forecasts indicate that this coming Sunday will bring an "early taste of summer" to the region, with temperatures projected to climb significantly above average. Residents should prepare for warm and sunny conditions that mark a premature arrival of the season's typical heat.</p>\n<p>Meteorologists at KSAT are tracking a weather pattern that will usher in a wave of unseasonably high temperatures, making Sunday feel more like mid-July than late spring or early summer. While many might welcome the warmth, it's a stark reminder to stay vigilant about heat safety.</p>\n<h3>Stay Safe and Hydrated</h3>\n<p>Authorities and health officials are urging the public to take necessary precautions. Hydration will be key throughout the day; residents are advised to drink plenty of water, even if not feeling thirsty. Limiting strenuous outdoor activities, especially during peak sun hours, and seeking shade or air-conditioned environments are also highly recommended.</p>\n<p>Pet owners should also ensure their animals have access to fresh water and shelter from the sun. With this early surge of summer-like weather, checking on vulnerable neighbors and family members is also a thoughtful consideration.</p>\n<p>While the full details of the forecast, including specific temperature highs and exact timing, will be refined in the coming days, the message is clear: Sunday will be a warm one. Embrace the sunshine responsibly and enjoy this unexpected preview of summer.</p>	Residents anticipate an unseasonably warm Sunday as temperatures soar, delivering an early taste of summer. Experts advise staying hydrated and taking precautions against the heat.	https://