748	Central NY Braces for Icy Commute After Weekend Rain	Central NY Braces for Icy Commute After Weekend Rain	central-ny-braces-for-icy-commute-after-weekend-rain	<p>Central New York is preparing for a potential weather challenge as a weekend of rain is forecast to give way to treacherous icy conditions by Monday morning. Authorities are urging residents to exercise extreme caution, especially during the morning commute.</p><p>According to weather reports, Sunday will see a significant amount of rainfall across the region. While the rain itself might not be disruptive, the crucial concern arises as temperatures are expected to drop overnight, potentially transforming wet surfaces into widespread ice.</p><h3>Hazardous Commute Expected</h3><p>The primary concern centers on Monday morning, when frozen precipitation could make roads and walkways extremely slick. Commuters are advised to anticipate difficult driving conditions, including black ice, which can be particularly perilous due to its invisibility.</p><p>Public safety officials recommend delaying travel if possible, allowing road crews time to treat surfaces. For those who must venture out, it is crucial to drive slowly, maintain increased following distances, and be extra vigilant for sudden changes in road conditions. Pedestrians should also be aware of slippery sidewalks and driveways.</p><p>Residents are encouraged to stay informed by monitoring local weather updates and advisories from their respective counties as the situation develops. Preparing for potential power outages and having emergency supplies on hand is also a prudent measure.</p>	Central New York residents are advised to prepare for hazardous travel conditions on Monday morning as weekend rain is expected to transition into icy roads, posing a significant risk for commuters.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1615238218358-4df2be7c224f?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxpY3ktcm9hZHMlMkMlMjB3aW50ZXItd2VhdG