393	Australian Senate Committee Greenlights Landmark Crypto Licensing Bill	Australian Senate Committee Greenlights Landmark Crypto Licensing Bill	australian-senate-committee-greenlights-landmark-crypto-licensing-bill	<h3>Australia Edges Closer to Comprehensive Crypto Regulation</h3><p>CANBERRA – A pivotal moment for digital asset regulation in Australia has arrived as the Australian Senate committee throws its weight behind a proposed bill that mandates licensing for cryptocurrency platforms. This endorsement marks a significant leap towards establishing a robust regulatory framework for the burgeoning crypto sector.</p><p>The Senate Economics Legislation Committee has recommended the passage of the Digital Assets (Market Regulation) Bill 2023, which aims to bring crypto exchanges and other digital asset service providers under the purview of existing financial services regulations. The core of the bill requires these platforms to obtain an Australian Financial Services (AFS) license, a move that would align them with traditional financial institutions.</p><p>Proponents of the bill argue that such regulation is crucial for <p><strong>enhancing consumer protection</strong></p> and mitigating risks associated with the volatile digital asset market. By mandating licensing, the government seeks to ensure transparency, accountability, and operational stability among crypto businesses. This also addresses concerns related to illicit financial activities and market manipulation.</p><p>While the industry has largely welcomed the clarity that regulation could bring, there remains an emphasis on ensuring that the framework fosters innovation rather than stifling it. The proposed legislation is expected to create a more secure and trustworthy environment for both retail and institutional investors engaging with cryptocurrencies.</p><p>The committee's recommendation paves the way for the bill to progress further through the parliamentary process. If enacted, Australia would join a growing list of nations implementing specific regulatory measures for digital assets, solidifying its position in the global effort to govern the evolving crypto landscape.</p>	Australia's Senate committee has endorsed a bill to license crypto platforms, signaling a major step towards comprehensive digital asset regulation and increased consumer protection across the nation.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518483239595-6f1f9e80b7c7?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxjcnlwdG8tcmVndWxhdGlvbiUyQyUyMGRpZ2l0YWwtZmluYW5jZSUyQyUyMGJsb2NrY2hhaW4tcG9saWN5fGVufDB8MHx8fDE3NzM2NDg4MDN8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	The Block	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxNdWJSd2RwWFIzZFJJczQ5MVZoUFBaSnIyRFczNEVVZnVCN2R3czU2WndCdzNHRFlLZmswMHBEQUdydUVfVm03V0xSYldqT1J0Q0RRM2JfSk11NEc0RTU3WWp6N3FWVlkwUklIZDJQZG9oS0hjQTROOHRwSUM2TG1hRXdzbU5Cc0J1d3A1THVOLVhTc2o5VVMwQy05dWswTjRnWk9ZN0YyRFJYbS02Wm9wclN3OGpUSGFDazVrSTdB?oc=5	\N	2026-03-16 08:13:23.461	2026-03-16 08:13:23.49977	Crypto	23
