328	Disney's 'Wish' Makes Theatrical Comeback After Strong Streaming Debut	Disney's 'Wish' Makes Theatrical Comeback After Strong Streaming Debut	disneys-wish-makes-theatrical-comeback-after-strong-streaming-debut	<p><strong>BURBANK, CA</strong> – Disney's latest animated feature, 'Wish', is set to return to select theaters for a limited engagement, a strategic move by the studio to reignite interest after the film garnered significant attention on its streaming platform, Disney+.</p><p>Initially released in November 2023, 'Wish' faced a challenging box office run, pulling in just $63.7 million domestically against a reported budget of $200 million. Despite its financial struggles and a mixed critical reception (holding a 57% score on Rotten Tomatoes), the film found a new audience and a surprising resurgence in popularity following its debut on Disney+ in April 2024. 'Wish' quickly ascended to become the platform's number one movie globally for two consecutive weeks, demonstrating strong viewer engagement.</p><p>This re-release strategy highlights Disney's evolving approach to film distribution, leveraging streaming success to provide a second wind for theatrical engagement. The decision comes as the studio continues to navigate the complex interplay between theatrical releases and streaming availability, especially for titles that may have underperformed initially but found a dedicated audience online.</p><h3>Why the Second Chance?</h3><p>The re-release offers an opportunity for families who enjoyed the film on Disney+ to experience it on the big screen, potentially boosting its overall revenue and solidifying its cultural footprint. It also allows Disney to test the waters on how streaming popularity can translate back into traditional cinema attendance.</p><p>As the entertainment industry continues to adapt to changing consumer habits, Disney's move with 'Wish' could serve as a model for future releases, demonstrating a more flexible and integrated approach to m