398	Coinbase Executive Slams New US Crypto Tax Rules as 'Disservice to People'	Coinbase Executive Slams New US Crypto Tax Rules as 'Disservice to People'	coinbase-executive-slams-new-us-crypto-tax-rules-as-disservice-to-people	<p>New U.S. crypto tax reporting regulations are drawing sharp criticism from industry leaders, with a Coinbase tax executive stating that the rules 'do a disservice to people.' Lawrence Zlatkin, VP of Global Tax at Coinbase, voiced concerns over the complexity and potential burden these regulations place on everyday cryptocurrency users, rather than primarily targeting illicit activities.</p>\n\n<h3>The Heart of the Criticism</h3>\n<p>The recently introduced rules aim to enhance transparency and ensure taxpayers accurately report their digital asset transactions. However, Zlatkin argues that the intricate nature of these requirements could overwhelm individuals, leading to confusion, errors, and potentially deterring participation in the legitimate crypto economy. He emphasized that while the intent to track taxable events is understood, the practical implementation could be overly onerous for the average person engaging in crypto.</p>\n\n<h3>Impact on Users and Innovation</h3>\n<p>Critics like Zlatkin fear that such stringent and complex reporting obligations could disproportionately affect retail investors and those simply using cryptocurrencies for legitimate purposes. The concern is that instead of fostering a clear regulatory environment, these rules could inadvertently push users towards less transparent platforms or discourage adoption altogether, stifling innovation within the U.S. digital asset space. Simplification and clearer guidance are often cited as essential for effective regulation that serves both government and citizens.</p>\n\n<h3>Industry's Call for Clarity</h3>\n<p>The crypto industry has consistently advocated for a collaborative approach with regulators to develop sensible and user-friendly tax frameworks. The sentimen