9	Saba and Cox Capital Launch Steep Discount Tender Offer for Blue Owl Private Credit Fund	Saba and Cox Capital Launch Steep Discount Tender Offer for Blue Owl Private Credit Fund	saba-and-cox-capital-launch-steep-discount-tender-offer-for-blue-owl-private-credit-fund	<p><strong>NEW YORK</strong> – In a significant move within the private credit market, investment firms Saba and Cox Capital Management have jointly launched a tender offer to acquire shares in one of Blue Owl's non-traded private credit funds. The offer stands at a notable 34.9% discount, highlighting strategic plays within the increasingly scrutinized alternative investment landscape.</p><p>This tender offer targets a specific segment of Blue Owl's extensive portfolio – its non-traded private credit funds. Such funds typically offer investors access to private debt opportunities, which can provide attractive yields but often come with liquidity constraints. The substantial discount proposed by Saba and Cox Capital Management suggests a strong interest in acquiring these assets at what they perceive to be a significant undervaluation, or perhaps to capitalize on a desire for liquidity among existing shareholders.</p><h3>Understanding the Tender Offer</h3><p>A tender offer is a public solicitation by a company or group to all shareholders of another company (or a specific fund in this case) to tender their stock for sale at a specified price during a particular time. In this instance, Saba and Cox are offering to purchase shares at nearly two-thirds of their reported net asset value (NAV), a discount that could be attractive to investors seeking immediate cash rather than holding an illiquid asset.</p><p>Private credit funds have seen immense growth in recent years, drawing capital from institutional and high-net-worth investors looking for diversification and higher returns outside traditional public markets. However, the non-traded nature of some of these funds means shares are not easily bought or sold on public exchanges, making liquidity an occasional challenge for investors.</p><h3>Market Implications</h3><p>The 34.9% discount is substantial and could reflect various factors, including market conditions, the specific performance or outlook of the Blue Owl fund in question, or a general repricing of illiquid assets. For Blue Owl, the offer could prompt a re-evaluation of its fund valuations and investor communication strategies. For Saba and Cox Capital, known for their activist and value-oriented investment approaches, this move represents a calculated effort to gain exposure to private credit assets at a distressed or opportunistic price point.</p><p>This development underscores the evolving dynamics within the private credit sector, where the balance between attractive yields and liquidity provisions continues to be a critical point of discussion for both fund managers and investors. The outcome of this tender offer will be closely watched as a potential indicator of future activity in the non-traded alternative investment space.</p>	Saba and Cox Capital Management have initiated a tender offer to acquire shares in a Blue Owl non-traded private credit fund, proposing a significant 34.9% discount, signaling potential market repositioning.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689330305908-aa231c1dd595?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxpbnZlc3RtZW50JTJDJTIwZmluYW5jZSUyQyUyMHByaXZhdGUtZXF1aXR5fGVufDB8MHx8fDE3NzMzMTI2MDR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	Financial News Wire	https://www.financialnewswire.com	\N	2026-03-12 10:50:04.377	2026-03-12 10:50:04.416126	Finance	37
28	Lilly Launches Platform to Simplify Obesity Treatment Benefits for Employers	Lilly Launches Platform to Simplify Obesity Treatment Benefits for Employers	lilly-launches-platform-to-simplify-obesity-treatment-benefits-for-employers	<p>In a significant stride towards optimizing corporate healthcare management, pharmaceutical leader Lilly has introduced an innovative platform designed to streamline how employers administer obesity treatment benefits. This new offering aims to provide a centralized hub for organizations to seamlessly connect with a diverse network of third-party program administrators, simplifying the complexities of managing treatment options and associated costs for their workforce.</p>\n\n<h3>Addressing the Challenge of Obesity Management</h3>\n<p>Obesity is increasingly recognized as a chronic disease requiring comprehensive and long-term care. For employers, navigating the myriad of treatment options, benefit structures, and administrative processes can be a daunting task. Lilly's platform directly addresses these challenges by consolidating resources and facilitating efficient communication between employers and specialized program administrators.</p>\n\n<h3>How the Platform Empowers Employers</h3>\n<p>The platform acts as a crucial intermediary, enabling employers to easily identify and engage with qualified third-party program administrators (TPAs) who specialize in various facets of obesity care. These administrators offer services ranging from nutritional counseling and lifestyle modification programs to access to advanced medications and bariatric surgery options. By centralizing these connections, the platform is poised to reduce administrative burdens, allowing employers to swiftly integrate effective and appropriate obesity management solutions into their employee benefits packages.</p>\n\n<h3>Driving Efficiency and Employee Well-being</h3>\n<p>For businesses, the key advantages include <strong>enhanced administrative efficiency</strong>, potential <strong>cost savings</strong> through optimized program selection, and greater transparency in benefit provision. The platform is designed to minimize the time and effort typically required to research, vet, and coordinate with multiple vendors. Ultimately, this initiative is expected to benefit employees by providing clearer, more accessible pathways to high-quality obesity treatment, fostering improved health outcomes, and contributing to overall employee well-being. Lilly's move underscores its commitment not only to pharmaceutical innovation but also to supporting the robust infrastructure needed for effective healthcare delivery in the modern corporate landscape.</p>	Lilly unveils a new platform for employers, simplifying connections with third-party administrators to manage obesity treatment benefits and costs efficiently for their employees.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1604480131833-5d7aea770e1c?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxjb3Jwb3JhdGUtaGVhbHRoJTJDJTIwaGVhbHRoY2FyZS1tYW5hZ2VtZW50JTJDJTIwZW1wbG95ZWUtYmVuZWZpdHN8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc3MzMxMzM1MXww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	Lilly Corporate News	https://www.lilly.com/newsroom	\N	2026-03-12 11:02:31.081	2026-03-12 11:02:31.125268	Business	41
