ive market sentiment. Projects that can garner community support and demonstrate utility or unique appeal often see amplified gains during such periods.</p>\n<p>Investors and enthusiasts are closely watching these developments, as the current market trajectory could signal further growth opportunities. However, the inherent volatility of cryptocurrencies dictates a cautious approach, even amidst exciting surges, reminding market participants of the importance of due diligence.</p>	The crypto market is buzzing as Bitcoin shows significant strength, driving other assets. Pepeto token marks a new milestone, reaching an $8 million valuation amidst the broader market surge.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1639825752750-5061ded5503b?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxjcnlwdG9jdXJyZW5jeSUyQyUyMGJpdGNvaW4lMkMlMjBtYXJrZXQtY2hhcnR8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc3Mzc2MzcxNnww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	TechBullion	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxPRjRCazRTdWp6cVF1ZXd3aWh3T2trSUc2clFMRklROXdpUmtjNFBfUGV2dlN3b1ZGVG84OTFkVFBZSy01T1p0bmZVdEJJMHNLOEJWck5IMnRlVkMzQ1BudFctaEJrV21tVm1LOEhtYzFQQk5JcXZfSUlMTGp3VzV6Z015THU?oc=5	\N	2026-03-17 16:08:36.368	2026-03-17 16:08:36.41804	Crypto	9
832	U.S. Lawmakers Introduce Bipartisan Bill to Ban Sports Betting on Prediction Markets	U.S. Lawmakers Introduce Bipartisan Bill to Ban Sports Betting on Prediction Markets	us-lawmakers-introduce-bipartisan-bill-to-ban-sports-betting-on-prediction-markets	<p>WASHINGTON D.C. – A bipartisan coalition of U.S. lawmakers has put forward a new bill designed to prohibit sports-related betting on prediction markets. The proposed legislation underscores growing concerns within Congress regarding the integrity of these nascent financial platforms and their intersection with the rapidly expanding sports betting industry.</p><h3>The Legislative Push Against Sports Prediction Markets</h3><p>The bill seeks to clarify the regulatory landscape by explicitly banning the use of prediction markets for wagering on sporting events. Prediction markets allow participants to bet on the outcome of future events, ranging from political elections to economic indicators. However, their application to sports has drawn scrutiny from lawmakers who fear potential avenues for manipulation, unfair practices, and a lack of adequate consumer protections.</p><p>Proponents of the bill argue that the unique structure of prediction markets, which often trade in contracts representing probabilities of outcomes, could create unforeseen risks when applied to sports. Unlike traditional sportsbooks operating under state-specific regulations, prediction markets often exist in a more ambiguous regulatory space, leading to calls for clearer guidelines.</p><h3>Implications for the Industry</h3><p>Should the bill pass, it would significantly impact companies currently offering or planning to offer sports-related contracts on their prediction market platforms. The move highlights a broader regulatory trend as lawmakers grapple with how to oversee innovative financial products that blur the lines between gambling, investing, and information aggregation.</p><p>While the sports betting industry continues its rapid expansion across the United States, this legislative effort signals a proactive approach by some policymakers to establish boundaries and ensure that new forms of wagering adhere to stringent ethical and consumer protection standards. The debate is expected to continue as the bill makes its way through the legislative process, with stakeholders on both sides poised to voice their perspectives on the future of prediction markets in the context of sports.</p>	A bipartisan group of U.S. lawmakers has introduced legislation aimed at banning sports betting activities on prediction markets, citing concerns over market integrity.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1620023652673-5820ac7aa64c?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxzcG9ydHMlMjBiZXR0aW5nJTJDJTIwbGVnaXNsYXRpb24lMkMlMjBwcmVkaWN0aW9uJTIwbWFya2V0c3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzc0MzU1NzQ3fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	WSJ	https://news.google.?oc=5	\N	2026-03-24 12:35:47.988	2026-03-24 12:35:48.069028	Finance	7
