192	China's Tech-Forward Strategy Shapes Future Economic Growth Post-'Two Sessions'	China's Tech-Forward Strategy Shapes Future Economic Growth Post-'Two Sessions'	chinas-tech-forward-strategy-shapes-future-economic-growth-post-two-sessions	<p>Beijing has concluded its annual 'Two Sessions' political meetings – the National People's Congress (NPC) and the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference (CPPCC) – charting a strategic course focused heavily on technological advancement and internal economic resilience. The sessions underscored China's intent to position itself as a pillar of global stability amidst ongoing international uncertainties and domestic economic adjustments.</p><p>A key outcome of the meetings was the announcement of a pragmatic economic growth target of 'around 5%' for the year. This objective is set to be achieved not through traditional growth drivers, but by prioritizing a dual-pronged strategy: supercharging domestic demand and accelerating breakthroughs in cutting-edge technologies. This strategic pivot signals a move away from export-reliant growth towards a more self-sufficient and innovation-driven economy.</p><h3>Innovation as the New Engine</h3><p>Central to China's forward-looking agenda is an aggressive push into new technologies. Discussions during the 'Two Sessions' highlighted the critical role of innovation in areas such as artificial intelligence, advanced manufacturing, and green energy. The government aims to foster an ecosystem where domestic enterprises can thrive and lead in technological fields, reducing reliance on external technologies and strengthening national competitiveness.</p><p>This tech-centric approach is seen as vital for creating new growth engines, upgrading traditional industries, and enhancing overall productivity. Policymakers stressed the importance of nurturing a skilled workforce and investing heavily in research and development to solidify China's position as a global technological powerhouse.</p><h3>Bolstering Domestic Demand and Global Standing</h3><p>Alongside technological innovation, boosting domestic demand remains a paramount objective. Measures are expected to be implemented to stimulate consumer spending and private investment, thereby creating a more robust internal market capable of withstanding global economic fluctuations. This focus on internal consumption is envisioned to provide a stable foundation for long-term economic prosperity.</p><p>Internationally, Chinese officials reiterated the nation's commitment to multilateralism and global cooperation, portraying China as a responsible major power dedicated to maintaining peace and stability. While addressing internal development, Beijing simultaneously sought to project an image of a reliable partner in a complex geopolitical landscape, subtly contrasting its approach with perceived global tensions.</p><p>As the 'Two Sessions' draw to a close, the world watches how China will implement these ambitious plans, particularly the synergy between technological innovation and domestic economic strength, to navigate both internal challenges and its evolving role on the global stage.</p>	Beijing concludes its annual 'Two Sessions,' signaling a robust commitment to technological innovation and domestic demand to achieve a pragmatic ~5% growth target and foster global stability.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1612672696056-770b18d7ba84?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxDaGluZXNlJTIwaW5ub3ZhdGlvbiUyQyUyMGVjb25vbWljJTIwc3RyYXRlZ3klMkMlMjB0ZWNoJTIwcG9saWN5fGVufDB8MHx8fDE3NzM0MTc3MzV8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	AP News	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxNS3ZpU3o3THVpX3Fkck1DRlFWUzZUbmpuWEwzMnlhMHRZanNsbUJlNngtTEk1RlVUZ0tlZTNTZUxVczUyc3VzVU9jMHN1Sy16M0NaUnFfd0tjUno0THpUX0pWMzNkRmtNOFZzNERyZDYxeURfdGd5Ri0zQ0hvaE9ka3hTWm4yZXppcVJJRElPRWpzdXZ0RWx1aFFTUXRzR1E3a0gwb2ZtczBiNExEV1E?oc=5	\N	2026-03-13 16:02:15.302	2026-03-13 16:02:15.341465	Technology	