485	Unveiling Qeshm: Iran's Underground Missile Base Amidst Geological Splendor	Unveiling Qeshm: Iran's Underground Missile Base Amidst Geological Splendor	unveiling-qeshm-irans-underground-missile-base-amidst-geological-splendor	<p>Qeshm Island, a gem nestled in the Strait of Hormuz, presents a striking duality: it is both a stunning testament to nature's artistry and a strategically vital underground missile fortress for Iran. This unique combination has drawn international attention, positioning Qeshm as a site of significant geopolitical and natural importance.</p><p><h3>A Geological Marvel</h3></p><p>Beyond its military fortifications, Qeshm Island is renowned for its extraordinary geological formations. Designated as Iran’s first UNESCO Global Geopark, the island boasts a diverse landscape of salt caves, dramatic canyons, and ancient valleys carved by millennia of natural processes. Its unique ecosystem supports a rich array of wildlife, including migratory birds and marine life, making it a hotspot for ecotourism and scientific study. The Hara forests, a rare mangrove ecosystem, further enhance its natural allure, attracting visitors keen to explore its pristine beauty and ecological diversity.</p><p><h3>The Hidden Fortress</h3></p><p>Beneath Qeshm's captivating surface lies a labyrinthine network of tunnels and bunkers, serving as a critical component of Iran's defense infrastructure. This underground missile fortress is designed to protect and launch various missile systems, offering a secure and concealed base for military operations in a highly sensitive region. The strategic location of Qeshm in the Strait of Hormuz, a crucial global oil transit chokepoint, amplifies the significance of this hidden facility, underscoring Iran's defensive capabilities and its posture in regional security dynamics.</p><p>The integration of advanced military technology within a naturally occurring geological structure highlights an innovative approach to defense. This subterranean complex is believed to be equipped with sophisticated command and control centers, logistics facilities, and hardened launchpads, providing a robust and resilient operational base largely impervious to conventional aerial surveillance or attack.</p><p>The story of Qeshm Island is a compelling narrative of contrast – where the timeless beauty of the natural world converges with cutting-edge military strategy. It remains a focal point for both environmental conservationists and geopolitical analysts, each group recognizing its profound, albeit different, significance.</p>	Qeshm Island in Iran stands as a remarkable paradox, blending breathtaking geological wonders with a hidden, strategic underground missile fortress, highlighting its dual significance.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1652563244384-700942b01ce4?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3w4OTMxMTJ8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwxfHxJcmFuJTIwUWVzaG0lMkMlMjBtaWxpdGFyeSUyMGZvcnRyZXNzJTJDJTIwZ2VvbG9naWNhbCUyMG1hcnZlbHxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzczNzMzNjM3fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080	Al Jazeera	https://news.google.?oc=5	\N	2026-03-17 07:47:17.182	2026-03-17 07:47:17.219231	Technology	8
817	Is AI Following the Dot-Com Bubble's Path? Lessons for the Modern Investor	Is AI Following the Dot-Com Bubble's Path? Lessons for the Modern Investor	is-ai-following-the-dot-com-bubbles-path-lessons-for-the-modern-investor	<p>The rapid ascent of artificial intelligence into nearly every facet of technology and business has sparked a familiar question among investors and analysts: Are we witnessing the formation of an 'AI bubble,' reminiscent of the infamous dot-com era?</p><p>The current landscape bears striking resemblances to the late 1990s, where internet companies, often with little more than a compelling idea and a 'dot-com' suffix, commanded exorbitant valuations. Today, the mere mention of 'AI' can send a company's stock soaring, regardless of its tangible products, profitability, or long-term viability. This speculative fervor has led many to draw parallels between the two periods, prompting a crucial examination of whether history is doomed to repeat itself.</p><h3>Echoes of the Past: Dot-Com Mania Revisited</h3><p>During the dot-com boom, irrational exuberance led to overvalued stocks, unsustainable business models, and ultimately, a painful market correction that wiped out trillions in wealth. Companies burned through capital with little return, focusing on user acquisition at any cost rather than sustainable growth. The initial promise of the internet was undeniable, but the market's inability to differentiate between genuine innovation and speculative ventures led to widespread losses.</p><p>Today, the AI sector exhibits similar characteristics. Valuations for AI startups and established tech giants heavily investing in AI have reached unprecedented levels. There's a rush to integrate AI into existing products or launch new AI-powered services, often with unproven monetization strategies. The fear of missing out (FOMO) drives investment decisions, sometimes overriding fundamental analysis.</p><h3>Distinguishing Genuine Innovation from Hype</h3><p>However, many argue that the current AI wave differs significantly from the dot-com bubble. Unlike many of the 'idea-stage' internet companies of the 90s, today's AI advancements are built on decades of research and development, backed by substantial computational power and vast datasets. The practical applications of AI are already evident across industries, from healthcare and finance to manufacturing and entertainment, demonstrating real-world value and productivity gains.</p><p>The challenge lies in discerning which AI ventures possess genuine long-term potential and which are merely riding the wave of hype. Investors are urged to look beyond buzzwords and focus on companies with clear business models, strong competitive advantages, robust intellectual property, and experienced leadership.</p><h3>Lessons for Prudent Investment</h3><p>To navigate this potentially volatile landscape, lessons from the dot-com era are invaluable:</p><ul><li><strong>Focus on Fundamentals:</strong> Prioritize companies with sound financials, sustainable revenue streams, and a clear path to profitability.</li><li><strong>Understand the Technology:</strong> Gain a basic understanding of the AI technology being developed and its realistic applications.</li><li><strong>Diversify Portfolios:</strong> Avoid overconcentration in a single sector, even one as promising as AI.</li><li><strong>Long-Term Vision:</strong> Invest with a long-term perspective, recognizing that disruptive technologies take time to mature and generate consistent returns.</li><li><strong>Beware of 'Greater Fool' Theory:</strong> Don't invest solely on the hope that someone else will pay more for an overvalued asset.</li></ul><p>While the transformative power of AI is undeniable, the current investment climate demands caution. By applying the wisdom gained from past market cycles, investors can better position themselves to capitalize on AI's promise while mitigating the risks of a potential bubble.</p>	As investments in 